{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "IEF", "bias": "BEARISH", "conviction": 0.35, "rationale": "Rates are the whole story: yields rose across the curve this week (5y +17bp, 10y +12bp) with the 10-year trading above 5% intraday and global yields at multi-decade highs, and a Fed hike is priced as near-certain. IEF is confirming that on the tape -- below 20/50/200d SMAs, 50d below 200d, sitting 4% off the 52-week low with negative MACD. Offsetting: RSI 31.8 is oversold, volume is light (0.56x), and short interest has rotated into the belly, so a hawkish-but-priced outcome could squeeze. Fundamentals are pure AA government paper at a 4.0% yield -- fine credit, no cushion against duration. Headlines describing '$7bn jackpot' bets on TLT are promotional noise and were not weighted; no analyst roll-up or positioning/flow data was provided, so those scores are left null.", "news_score": -0.4, "technical_score": -0.45, "fundamental_score": -0.1, "analyst_score": 0.0, "insider_score": 0.0, "key_factors": ["10-year yield 4.96%, +12bp on the week; 5-year +17bp, curve bear-flattening in the belly", "10-year traded above 5% intraday amid multi-decade-high global yields", "Price 91.12 below 20d/50d/200d SMAs with 50d under 200d, 4.3% of the way up the 52-week range", "RSI(14) 31.8 and 0.56x average volume argue against chasing the break", "Dollar index +0.92 on the week, consistent with hawkish repricing"]}, "result": {"status": "ACCEPTED", "ticker": "IEF", "bias": "BEARISH", "conviction": 0.35, "reason": "submitted sell 131 IEF @ ~91.12, stop 91.87", "quantity": 131, "side": "sell", "entry_price": 91.125, "stop_price": 91.87, "atr": 0.3712447039220718, "order_id": "f5c95620-92e0-4199-a4e8-a385b9d4d45f", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T16:04:28.098626Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-16 16:04:28,098", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "TLT", "bias": "BEARISH", "conviction": 0.35, "rationale": "Yields rose across the curve this week (5y +17bp, 10y +12bp) with the 10-year breaking 5%, and TLT sits at 81.11, within 0.5% of its 52-week low, below its 20/50/200d SMAs with 50d under 200d and negative MACD. A Fed hike is priced for Wednesday, which is a hostile backdrop for duration. The $7bn inflow headline is a crowded contrarian long into that event rather than evidence of a turn, and the 'jackpot' framing is promotional; I weigh flows as crowding, not direction. Bond-market regime is bearish but the hike is largely priced and RSI near 40 with low volume limits conviction; a dovish surprise would sharply reverse this.", "news_score": -0.35, "technical_score": -0.5, "fundamental_score": -0.1, "analyst_score": 0.0, "insider_score": -0.2, "key_factors": ["10-year Treasury yield broke 5%, highest since 2007; 5y +17bp on the week", "TLT at 81.11, only 3.6% up from 52-week low, below 20/50/200d SMAs with 50d<200d", "Fed decision priced as near-certain rate hike", "$7bn crowded speculative inflow into TLT ahead of the decision reads as positioning risk, not signal", "Dollar index +0.92 on the week, curve normalizing steeper at +1.02"]}, "result": {"status": "ACCEPTED", "ticker": "TLT", "bias": "BEARISH", "conviction": 0.35, "reason": "submitted sell 147 TLT @ ~81.11, stop 82.41", "quantity": 147, "side": "sell", "entry_price": 81.1050033569336, "stop_price": 82.41, "atr": 0.6549425928114492, "order_id": "e6477572-a86f-4637-8e15-2487c81aaa18", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T16:05:07.404112Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-16 16:05:07,404", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
